ences fast a as  well as annotation and associated files  right here at the NCBI human genome  resources page and with that I am happy  to stop and take any questions that you  may have so somebody who has where we  could where you can find the common list  of variants reported in all ncbi  resources and i would say that if you're  looking for short variants variants  under 50 nucleotides you're going to  want to look in DB snip and in fact for  the DB snip grch38 release that's really  going to be a VCF of all of those  variants similarly if you're interested  in structural variants you're going to  want the latest DV bar release and so  and like I said both of those resources  are available right here on the human  genome resources page so there's some  specific questions I will take a look at  them and we may answer some of them  offline yeah well we'll actually put  them in the documentation for the  webinar  all right we're going to go ahead and  wrap it up thank you very much for your  time and I hope you have an excellent  rest of the day  you
 

